":12.8},"placed_piece_count":234,"unplaced_submodels":[{"file":"cm-palace-hall.ldr","status":"local_definition_not_root_reachable","design_review":{"scope":"B-owned Round Table Hall; shared root placement remains main-owned. No cathedral or other department geometry is included.","local_floor":"24 x 24 stud base; visible floor top at local Y=0 LDU and floor stud plane Y=-8 LDU.","front_entry":"Closed front wall retained. Centered 2-stud clear opening through full wall depth, built jambs and timber lintel; clear height 6 brick courses. The table and interior seating remain partially visible through the opening.","table_and_seats":"Round tabletop approximated by four real 2x2 round LEGO bricks. Twelve inward-facing knight seats plus one distinct raised red/gold empty perilous seat at the rear.","roof_mechanism":"Two upward-removable gable cassettes split at the ridge, each assigned to a B group. Shallow 30363 slope rows, three longitudinal 3034 stringers plus two lower overlap ties, ridge locators, and an 8-stud reinforced brick grasp rail. Wall footprint 24x24; eaves overhang one stud at the sides.","closure":"Six discrete 1x1 wall pads per cassette provide nominal eave seating and partial stud locks; ridge rails meet in alignment. B local saved pose is CLOSED.","chandelier":"Four-arm chandelier is connected beneath B-roof-left and lifts with that cassette. B-roof-right carries no pendant.","removal_review":"Digital vertical lift has no hinge sweep or undercut. Removing either roof leaves the hall and remaining roof as one supported component; removing both leaves the hall, furniture and fixed pads as one component. Top access opens after lifting.","checks":{"default_closed":{"parts":546,"supported_components":1,"stud_grid_matches":3044,"unsupported_parts":0},"left_roof_plus_chandelier":{"parts":106,"supported_components":1},"right_roof":{"parts":89,"supported_components":1},"hall_after_both_roofs_removed":{"parts":351,"supported_components":1},"hall_after_either_sin